---
title: "Copy feedback"
description: "Every kind of copy mistake an AI has caught on this site, with the rule behind it and one example each."
---
<style>{% include "css/copy-feedback.css" %}</style>

<h1>Copy feedback</h1>

<p>I run drafts past an AI copyeditor before publishing. Mechanical mistakes — spelling, punctuation, agreement, house style — get fixed straight away. Anything that would change how I sound I decide on myself, and those decisions stay off this page.</p>

<p>This is the index of what it caught, grouped by rule with one example each. The point is to learn the rule, not to count my typos. Every entry names a source, because you shouldn’t take an AI’s word for a correction and neither should I.</p>

{%- if collections.copyLessons.length %}
{%- for category, lessons in collections.copyLessons | groupby("category") %}
<h2>{{ category | title }}</h2>

{%- for lesson in lessons %}
<div class="copy-lesson">
	<p class="copy-lesson-change diff">
		<span aria-hidden="true">{{ lesson.before | inlineDiff(lesson.after) | safe }}</span>
		<span class="visually-hidden">Before: {{ lesson.before }}. After: {{ lesson.after }}.</span>
	</p>
	<p class="copy-lesson-why">{{ lesson.why | smartquotes }}</p>
	<p class="copy-lesson-meta"><span class="copy-lesson-source">{{ lesson.source | smartquotes }}</span> · first seen in <a href="{{ lesson.firstSeenUrl }}">{{ lesson.firstSeenTitle }}</a>{% if lesson.count > 1 %} · <span class="copy-lesson-count">caught {{ lesson.count }} times</span>{% endif %}</p>
</div>
{%- endfor %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- else %}
<p>Nothing caught yet.</p>
{%- endif %}
